# PDF -> Markdown conversion

Any PDF (`.pdf`) to Markdown (`.md`) conversion performed in this repository —
whether the agent is recovering text from a vendor datasheet, importing a spec
that only exists as PDF, or extracting diagrams/images from a PDF for inclusion
in repo docs — **must** use the shared helper
`scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py` instead of invoking `pdftotext`,
`pdfimages`, `PyMuPDF` (`fitz`), `pdfplumber`, or any other PDF-parsing
library directly.

`scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py` is cross-platform (macOS, RHEL,
Ubuntu) and location-agnostic. It already encapsulates the repo conventions:
text extraction with heading/list/structure preservation, image/diagram
extraction into a sibling `images/` directory, Markdown image references with
relative paths, and a graceful fallback chain
(`PyMuPDF` -> `pdfplumber` -> poppler system tools `pdftotext` / `pdfimages`).

## When to use it

- Converting a `.pdf` file (or several, one invocation at a time) to Markdown.
- Recovering text + diagrams from a PDF-only spec / datasheet / report so it
  can be checked into the repo as `.md`.
- Extracting images from a PDF for reuse in repo documentation.

## When NOT to use it

- Markdown -> PDF (the other direction) — use `scripts/build_docs.sh` (see
  the `md-to-pdf.mdc` rule).
- AsciiDoc (`.adoc`) sources — this script is PDF-input only.
- Re-flowing or re-styling an existing `.md` — edit the `.md` directly.
- OCR of scanned/image-only PDFs — this script extracts the embedded text
  layer and images; it does not run OCR. If a PDF has no text layer, request
  an OCR-capable tool instead.

## Invocation patterns

```bash
# Default: .md written next to the .pdf (same basename, .md extension),
# images extracted into <pdf_dir>/images/.
python3 scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py doc/foo.pdf
#   -> doc/foo.md
#   -> doc/images/page_1_img_1.png, ...

# Explicit output file path.
python3 scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py doc/foo.pdf doc/foo_out.md

# Explicit output directory (trailing slash matters — without it the path
# is treated as a file name). The .md is named after the PDF basename.
python3 scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py doc/foo.pdf -o build/

# Dependency check (no conversion; prints which backends are available).
python3 scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py --check-deps

# Help:
python3 scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py -h
```

Always invoke with `python3` (not `python`) for portability across macOS,
RHEL, and Ubuntu.

## Dependencies

The script auto-detects whichever backend is installed and falls back through
a chain, so install **any one** of:

- **PyMuPDF** (preferred, best image extraction):
  - `pip install PyMuPDF`  (any platform)
- **pdfplumber** (text-only fallback — images will come from `pdfimages`):
  - `pip install pdfplumber`
- **poppler system tools** (last-resort fallback, no Python deps):
  - macOS:  `brew install poppler`
  - RHEL:   `sudo dnf install poppler-utils`
  - Ubuntu: `sudo apt-get install poppler-utils`

Run `python3 scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py --check-deps` to see
which backends are currently available on the host.

## Rules

- Do **not** run `pdftotext`, `pdfimages`, `pdfplumber`, or `PyMuPDF` directly
  to produce Markdown — call the script so the image-extraction layout,
  relative image paths, and heading heuristics stay consistent across the
  repo.
- Do **not** hand-write a new `pdf2md_*.py` per document. New conversions go
  through `scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py`.
- If the script is missing a capability you need (better table handling,
  OCR fallback, alternate image naming, page-range selection), **extend
  `scripts/pdf_to_markdown_with_diagrams.py`** rather than duplicating it.
- After conversion, **check the produced `.md`** before reporting success:
  the script prints `Markdown saved to: <path>` and `Output size: N bytes`.
  Image-only or scanned PDFs will produce a near-empty `.md` — flag that to
  the user rather than presenting an empty conversion as success.
- The script writes images into an `images/` subdirectory **relative to the
  output `.md` location**, and the `.md` references them with relative paths
  (`images/page_N_img_M.<ext>`). Do not move the `.md` without the `images/`
  directory, or the references will break.

